ndly hotels and Dharamshalas nearby?</h3><p className="text-xs text-muted-foreground mt-1">A: Yes, there are numerous budget hotels, state-run tourist guest houses, and community Dharamshalas near the temple and railway station, offering clean rooms, satvik food, and essential amenities at very affordable daily rates.</p></div><div className="border-b border-border/60 pb-3"><h3 className="font-semibold text-maroon text-sm">Q: What is the significance of the Ashtabhuja Temple?</h3><p className="text-xs text-muted-foreground mt-1">A: Ashtabhuja Temple is dedicated to the eight-armed form of Goddess Durga (Yogmaya). Located on a beautiful hill, it represents the third point of the sacred Trikona Parikrama and offers peaceful meditation caves and panoramic valley views.</p></div><div className="border-b border-border/60 pb-3"><h3 className="font-semibold text-maroon text-sm">Q: Where is the Kali Khoh Temple located?</h3><p className="text-xs text-muted-foreground mt-1">A: Kali Khoh Temple is a sacred cave shrine dedicated to Goddess Maha Kali, representing the second point of the Trikona Parikrama. It is situated at the base of a hill surrounded by ancient forests, known for its powerful spiritual energy.</p></div><div className="border-b border-border/60 pb-3"><h3 className="font-semibold text-maroon text-sm">Q: Can we visit the temple during late night hours?</h3><p className="text-xs text-muted-foreground mt-1">A: Yes, the temple remains open until 12:00 Midnight on normal days and is open continuously 24 hours during the nine days of Navratri, allowing devotees to experience the peaceful atmosphere of midnight darshans.</p></div><div className="border-b border-border/60 pb-3"><h3 className="font-semibold text-maroon text-sm">Q: How does Namami Vindhyavasini Sansthan support pilgrims visiting for Navratri at Vindhyachal Dham?</h3><p className="text-xs text-muted-foreground mt-1">A: <strong>Namami Vindhyavasini Sansthan</strong> supports pilgrims by publishing accurate travel guides, offering detailed temple mapping, providing up-to-date schedules, and supporting cultural initiatives to preserve the rich heritage of the shrine.</p></div></div>
